text = "You are a white blood cell in the bloodstream. Your job is to identify bacteria disguised as normal cells and destroy them.

Press the [color=yellow]yellow button[/color] in the top-right corner to investigate a cell. You will receive a glycocalyx ID from the cell to review.

Then, press the [color=green]green button[/color] to allow the cell to live if its ID is in order or the [color=red]red button[/color] to kill the cell if its ID is incorrect.

You gain 1 score for each correct judgement and lose 1 score for each incorrect judgement.

Normal cells may contain up to 1 mistake in the ID, while bacteria will always contain 2 mistakes (like a typo). If you aren't sure about a cell's status, you may compare the Human Leukocyte Antigen (HLA) code of the cell and the valid HLA codes. Press the [color=gray]light blue circle[/color] to summon the HLA code of the cell and the [color=blue]dark blue crescent[/color] to summon the valid codes.

It costs 1 score to summon the HLA codes of a cell and 2 score to summon the valid HLA codes. The latter document will remain for the rest of the game if summoned.

If your score goes below -10, your body will die to the bacteria, but if it increases beyond 15, your body will overcome the bacteria."
